== o6_tower ==

-- P1: passive tower on the dyadic grid
P1  elementary arcs reachable as intersections of two grid half-circles: True; table ranks m = 1..6: [3, 5, 9, 17, 33, 65] (2^m + 1: [3, 5, 9, 17, 33, 65])  -> True

-- K: the re-preparing (cosine-law) tower on the circle
K1  P(+u | rho_psi) - (1 + cos beta)/2 on [0, pi]: 0; on [pi, 2 pi]: 0; normalization 1; density cos(s)/2 >= 0 on (-pi/2, pi/2)  -> True
K2  table rank (single and two-step readouts) at stages n = 1..10: [3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3]  -> True
K3  minimal polynomial of (3+4i)/5: 5*x**2 - 6*x + 5 (monic over Z: False); R(a)^k != 1 for k = 1..200: True  -> True
K4  stages n = 1..20: directions distinct, g(stage n) in stage n+1 and (n+1)a not in stage n: True
K5  repeatable on stage directions: True; observe-and-forget along u = 0 sends (Fraction(3, 5), Fraction(4, 5)) to (Fraction(3, 5), Fraction(0, 1)): invasive True; frame readout outcome-random on rho_(ka), k = 1..200: True  -> True
K6  closure member R(pi/2): (P_coh, P_deph) = (1, 1/2); stage data g^k, k = 1..200: P_deph = (1 + cos^2 ka)/2 > 1/2 for all: True  -> True

-- K7: the ball (sphere substratum, cosine law)
K7  projection area - (pi/2 + (pi/2) cos beta) == 0: True (so P(+u|rho_psi) = (1 + psi.u)/2); table rank on 18 rational unit vectors: 4; OFF-Gamma' for m = 1..60: True  -> True

-- K8, K9: what finite rank asks of the re-preparation law
K8  uniform law (response 1 - |beta|/pi) on the dyadic grid, ranks m = 1..6: [3, 5, 9, 17, 33, 65]  -> True
K9  degree-1 responses with f(0) = 1, f(beta) + f(beta + pi) = 1: [{c0: 1/2, c1: 1/2}] (Born response forced: True); degree-3 response repeatable: True, density = -f'(t + pi/2): True, density = (3/4) cos^3 t >= 0: True, table rank on 17 Pythagorean directions: 5  -> True

-- countercontrols (must be False)
CC1  CC-OK (False as required)
CC2  CC-OK (False as required)
CC3  CC-OK (False as required)
CC4  CC-OK (False as required)
CC5  CC-OK (False as required)

  K1: True
  K2: True
  K3: True
  K4: True
  K5: True
  K6: True
  K7: True
  K8: True
  K9: True
  P1: True
VERDICT EXCLUSIVE-ON-PASSIVE-JOINT-ON-INVASIVE: on the circle substratum the passive tower's rank grows with
  the stage (P1), as the theorem requires of any passive tower carrying an infinite-order datum; the
  re-preparing tower has rank 3 at every stage, an infinite-order stage-crossing datum, a repeatable and
  invasive readout and the exact witness in the closure (K1-K6); the ball version adds OFF (K7); finite rank
  constrains the re-preparation law (K8) and minimal rank forces the response (1 + cos beta)/2 (K9).
